fix(azure): align Foundry staging endpoint contract

Purpose
Make the declarative Azure staging contract match the verified Azure AI Services account and deployment used by the running agent.

Changes
- Parameterize the existing Foundry account and deployment names in Bicep.
- Default staging to aegisbankstagingai and phi-4-mini-instruct.
- Emit the Cognitive Services endpoint used by the AzureOpenAI managed-identity client.
- Update the staging acceptance runbook with the verified endpoint and deployment.

Validation
- az bicep build --file deploy/azure/main.bicep --stdout: PASS.
- Focused pytest for agent API and Azure Foundry tests: PASS (15 passed).
- Ruff check and format check for changed Python files: PASS.
- Public staging GET /health/live and /health/ready: PASS (HTTP 200).
- Azure model deployment state: Succeeded; direct synthetic completion returned OK.
- git diff --check: PASS.

Limitations
- Container Apps CLI updates remain temporarily unavailable while Microsoft.App provider registration is still propagating; the live agent environment was updated through the Azure management API.
- Full authenticated agent acceptance remains blocked until an approved Entra JWT audience and synthetic customer claim are configured.
